This example is f90_mpif with the mpi module (use mpi) instead of
include "mpif.h".

NOTE: As of SALT-FM v0.6.0, the only supported build is to build this example
and the MPI implementation with the same Flang that SALT-FM uses. With any
other compiler, this example is expected to fail. Support for "use mpi" with
other compilers is planned for SALT-FM v0.7.0, which should be out soon.

The Makefile sets SALT_BUILD_USES_SALT_FLANG=1, which tells SALT-FM to read
the .mod files from the build and from MPI. To use it:
$ export TAU_MAKEFILE=<taudir>/x86_64/lib/Makefile.tau-clang-mpi
$ ./run.sh

The mpi_f08 module also builds this way, but TAU does not wrap the mpi_f08
MPI_Init, so every rank writes profile.0.0.0.
